ument>\n[Your Name]\n[Address] · [Phone] · [Email]\n\n[Date]\n\nKaren Doyle\nHR Manager\nCalder Pharmaceuticals\nWestfield, [State]\n\nDear Ms. Doyle,\n\nI am applying for the Training Coordinator position at Calder Pharmaceuticals' Westfield plant. I have taught high school chemistry for nine years. Much of that work has been what a training coordinator does: designing safety training, delivering it, documenting it and checking that it worked.\n\nIn 2019 I wrote my school's lab safety program. Since then, no one in our labs has had an injury that needed more than first aid. The program keeps a signed record for every student's lab safety quiz and for every new teacher I train. The state has audited those records twice and found nothing. I know GMP training records are a different standard, and I won't pretend I've already met it. I have enrolled in an online GMP basics course that finishes in May. I also already have the habit the role depends on: no one does the work until their training is complete and documented.\n\nI also train our new science teachers on lab procedures, about two a year. In 2020 I rebuilt that training and cut it from 20 hours to 12. I kept the content that mattered and dropped what didn't. I'd bring the same approach to Calder's onboarding. I would learn what each part of the training is there to do, keep everything that's required and make the rest faster and easier to retain.\n\nTeaching 140 students a year has taught me to explain technical material to people who start at very different levels, and to measure whether they actually learned it. Over the four years I have taught AP Chemistry, our pass rate rose from 41% to 58%.\n\nMy classes run on Google Classroom, and I haven't used Calder's learning management system yet. I expect to learn it quickly, and I'll be ready to keep accurate records in it from the start. I live about 30 minutes from Westfield.\n\nI would welcome the chance to talk about how I can support your training program. Thank you for your consideration.\n\nSincerely,\n[Your Name]\n</final_document>\n\nBefore you send it:\n- **Date the course.** \"Finishes in May\" assumes May 2027. Use the full date if that reads better to you.\n- **Add a reason for the move.** The letter has none beyond the short commute. If you have one, even \"I want to train adults in work where the stakes are high,\" add it to the last paragraph. Hiring managers who see a career change often wonder why.","ttft_ms":5327,"type":"result","duration_ms":14627,"uuid":"c9f3b7fd-6c71-44de-9224-ea85b012d838","ttft_stream_ms":1416,"time_to_request_ms":153,"first_content_frame_ms":1416,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":1242,"cacheReadInputTokens":9944,"cacheCreationInputTokens":901,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0340528,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":359,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":901,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"credential_expires_at":"2026-12-07T10:02:13.271Z"}
